## API Development

### ✅ DO

| Rule | Implementation |
|------|----------------|
| Validate ALL input | At API boundary |
| Parameterized queries | Never string concatenation |
| Centralized errors | Consistent error format |
| HTTPS everywhere | Security first |
| Rate limiting | Protect endpoints |

### ❌ DON'T

| Rule | Why |
|------|-----|
| Trust user input | Validate everything |
| Expose internal errors | Return safe messages only |
| Hardcode secrets | Use env vars |
| Giant controllers | Split into services |

---

## Security Rules

| ✅ DO | ❌ DON'T |
|-------|----------|
| Hash passwords (bcrypt/argon2) | Store plain text |
| Verify JWT signature | Trust JWT without verify |
| Check authorization every route | Skip auth checks |
| Use HTTPS everywhere | HTTP in production |
| Implement CORS properly | Allow all origins |

---

## Architecture

- **Layered architecture**: Controller → Service → Repository
- **Dependency injection** for testability
- **Centralized error handling**
- **Appropriate logging** (no sensitive data)

---

## Quality Control Loop

After editing any file:
1. `npm run lint && npx tsc --noEmit`
2. Security check: No hardcoded secrets, input validated
3. Type check: No TypeScript/type errors
4. Test: Critical paths have coverage

---

## Anti-Patterns

| ❌ Don't | ✅ Do |
|---------|-------|
| SQL Injection | Parameterized queries, ORM |
| N+1 Queries | JOINs, DataLoader, includes |
| Blocking Event Loop | Async for I/O |
| Express for Edge | Hono/Fastify |
| Skipping auth check | Verify every protected route |
| Hardcoded secrets | Environment variables |
